"div",null,{"className":"font-serif text-base md:text-lg text-text-primary","children":"Member-Level Sell-Through Data"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"font-sans text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed","children":"Monthly dispense, adherence, prescriber attribution, and program performance reports delivered through the platform reporting portal. This is data the standard distributor channel structurally cannot provide: sell-through, not sell-in."}]]}]]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-navy","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-content mx-auto px-6 md:px-12 py-16 md:py-24","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 lg:gap-16 mb-14","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans text-eyebrow uppercase text-white/[0.35] block mb-4","children":"Platform Architecture"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[28px] md:text-[36px] lg:text-[42px] text-white leading-[1.15] tracking-tight-display","children":"Three Engines. One Integrated System."}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-base text-white/50 leading-body lg:pt-8","children":"Built on a patent-pending architecture that handles every function from prescription intake to supplier payment. No existing distribution model, specialty pharmacy, or compliance tool has combined these capabilities in a single platform."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-0","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-white/[0.07] pt-8 pb-8 lg:pr-8","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xs text-orange tracking-[0.06em] block mb-4","children":"01"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[19px] text-white leading-[1.3] mb-4","children":"Prescription and Member Engagement Engine"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-sm text-white/[0.45] leading-relaxed","children":"Receives electronic prescriptions via NCPDP SCRIPT from any intake pathway. Verifies member eligibility in real time. Initiates a single member interaction via SMS for pharmacy selection and cost-share collection. Executes prescription transfer. Initiates the four-event settlement sequence."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-white/[0.07] pt-8 pb-8 lg:px-8 lg:border-l","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xs text-orange tracking-[0.06em] block mb-4","children":"02"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[19px] text-white leading-[1.3] mb-4","children":"Multi-Channel Lowest Net Cost Routing Engine"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-sm text-white/[0.45] leading-relaxed","children":"Evaluates every in-scope prescription against all plan-activated supply channel categories in real time: manufacturer-direct, standard PBM channel, platform pharmacy supplier. Selects the lowest net cost option. This is a routing decision across categorically distinct supply chain architectures, not a selection among pharmacies within a single channel."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-white/[0.07] pt-8 pb-8 lg:pl-8 lg:border-l","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xs text-orange tracking-[0.06em] block mb-4","children":"03"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[19px] text-white leading-[1.3] mb-4","children":"Distribution and DSCSA Compliance Engine (Patent Pending)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-sm text-white/[0.45] leading-relaxed","children":"Manages the serialized virtual pre-allocation pool for manufacturer-direct custodial inventory. Generates DSCSA-compliant per-prescription T3 documentation at the individual dispense level without a change-of-ownership trigger at the 3PL. Administers just-in-time replenishment against the enrolled member census. Provisional patent filed March 2026."}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-off-white","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-content mx-auto px-6 md:px-12 py-16 md:py-24","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans text-eyebrow uppercase text-orange block mb-4","children":"Commercial Structure"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[28px] md:text-[36px] lg:text-[42px] text-text-primary leading-[1.15] tracking-tight-display mb-10","children":"Transparent, Auditable Economics"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12 pb-12 border-b border-border","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[32px] md:text-[38px] text-navy tracking-tight-display leading-none mb-2","children":"WAC Preserved"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-[13px] text-text-secondary","children":"Across all channels"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[32px] md:text-[38px] text-navy tracking-tight-display leading-none mb-2","children":"One Counterparty"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-[13px] text-text-secondary","children":"One invoice. One payment."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[32px] md:text-[38px] text-navy tracking-tight-display leading-none mb-2","children":"< 30 Days"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-[13px] text-text-secondary","children":"Inventory dwell time at 3PL"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 md:gap-16","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-serif text-lg text-text-primary mb-3","children":"Pricing mechanism"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed","children":"The manufacturer invoices at WAC. A per-drug employer-direct program rebate, defined in the master supply agreement, is applied as a line deduction on the monthly invoice. Net payment is WAC minus the rebate. This structure preserves most-favored-nation integrity because manufacturer rebates are almost universally excluded from MFN calculations under existing contracts."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-serif text-lg text-text-primary mb-3","children":"Data exchange"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-sans text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed","children":"ApalyRx provides monthly member-level utilization reporting, adherence metrics, prescriber attribution, and program performance data through the platform portal. This is sell-through visibility, actual dispense events at the member level, that the traditional distributor channel structurally cannot provide."}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-white","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-content mx-auto px-6 md:px-12 py-16 md:py-24","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans text-eyebrow uppercase text-orange block mb-4","children":"Common Questions"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[28px] md:text-[36px] lg:text-[42px] text-text-primary leading-[1.15] tracking-tight-display mb-12","children":"Answers for Every Internal Stakeholder"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl","children":["$","$L4",null,{"sections":[{"title":"Operations Team","items":[{"question":"Does this require new logistics or warehouse infrastructure?","answer":"No. The manufacturer's one new operational step is shipping to an ApalyRx-designated 3PL facility rather than a distributor warehouse. ApalyRx owns and manages the 3PL relationship entirely. All documentation and downstream fulfillment are handled by ApalyRx."},{"question":"Do we need new DSCSA systems?","answer":"No. The manufacturer provides serialization data per current procedures. The ApalyRx platform handles all per-script T3 documentation as a technology service. No manufacturer system builds required."},{"question":"Who manages cold chain during transit?","answer":"The manufacturer ships to the ApalyRx-designated 3PL using existing cold chain protocols. ApalyRx bears responsibility for cold chain management from the 3PL forward. Cold chain standards are contractual obligations in the ApalyRx-3PL service agreement."}]},{"title":"Finance Team","items":[{"question":"How does revenue recognition work?","answer":"Revenue is recognized at point of title transfer, confirmed home delivery or physical receipt at the participating pharmacy. This is a discrete, documentable event recorded by the ApalyRx platform. The monthly invoice reflects all title transfer events in the prior month."},{"question":"What is our credit exposure?","answer":"The manufacturer's counterparty is ApalyRx. Credit exposure is evaluated against ApalyRx as the contracting entity. The manufacturer has no direct financial relationship with any health plan."},{"question":"How does this interact with gross-to-net?","answer":"WAC is preserved. The per-drug program rebate is a separately documented supply agreement benefit. GTN for this channel is calculated as WAC minus the rebate, with no chargebacks, no distributor fees. Structurally cleaner than the standard rebate chain."}]},{"title":"Legal Team","items":[{"question":"Does this create new wholesale distribution obligations?","answer":"No. The 3PL is a licensed third-party logistics provider, not a wholesale distributor. Custody transfer to the 3PL without title transfer does not trigger wholesale distribution requirements under DSCSA or state law."},{"question":"Does the manufacturer contract with health plans?","answer":"No. The manufacturer's only counterparty is ApalyRx. Employer demand is transmitted by proxy through ApalyRx as the authorized channel operator. The manufacturer has no direct employer relationships to establish or defend."},{"question":"Will this trigger MFN provisions?","answer":"The WAC with employer-direct program rebate structure is designed to avoid triggering MFN provisions. WAC is preserved across all channels. Manufacturer legal teams should validate the specific MFN language in their PBM contracts against this structure."}]},{"title":"Commercial and Market Access Team","items":[{"question":"Is this a pilot program?","answer":"No. This is a live channel infrastructure built and operated by ApalyRx. 3PL fulfillment, DSCSA documentation systems, pharmacy credentialing across 50 states, and plan contracting are all operational today. The inaugural employer deployment is a live validation of a complete operational system, not a proof of concept."},{"question":"How does this affect existing PBM relationships?","answer":"The program is designed to function alongside existing PBM benefits. Health plans direct specific high-cost specialty drugs through the program while maintaining their PBM for the broader formulary. The manufacturer's existing formulary arrangements for all other drugs are unchanged."},{"question":"What does the manufacturer gain that no other channel provides?","answer":"Real-time member-level sell-through data, prescriber attribution, adherence metrics, and locked formulary position within employer-configured drug programs, combined with rebates applied at dispense rather than held 90 to 180 days by intermediaries."}]}]}]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-off-white","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-content mx-auto px-6 md:px-12 py-16 md:py-24","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans text-eyebrow uppercase text-orange block mb-4","children":"Implementation"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[28px] md:text-[36px] lg:text-[42px] text-text-primary leading-[1.15] tracking-tight-display mb-12","children":"Operational in Six Months"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-6 gap-6","children":[["$","div","1",{"className":"border-t-2 border-orange pt-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xs text-orange tracking-[0.06em] block mb-1","children":["Phase ","1"]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans text-xs text-text-muted block mb-2","children":"Months 1–2"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-serif text-base 